<title>BELGIUM: Belgian money market supply cut in week.</title>
<headline>Belgian money market supply cut in week.</headline>
<dateline>BRUSSELS 1996-12-31</dateline>
<text>
<p>The Belgian National Bank said it withdrew liquidity from the money market in the week to December 30 mainly due to a decrease in the amount of repos outstanding and interbank loans.</p>
<p>(figures from the weekly statement in bln francs) -</p>
<p> Foreign currency reserves	   418.86 (-  0.01)</p>
<p> Advances against pledged security  21.30 (+  4.42)</p>
<p> Commercial bills			  2.75 (-  0.50)</p>
<p> Securities portfolio		   24.82 (unch)</p>
<p> Money market interventions*	 115.65 (-  7.98)</p>
<p> Bank notes in circulation	   468.48 (-  4.26)</p>
<p>* comprises repurchase agreements and interbank loans</p>
<p>-- Brussels Newsroom +32 2 287 6810, Fax +32 2 230 7710</p>
</text>
